pr_body:
- [x] Depends on https://github.com/ppy/osu/pull/24965
- [x] ~~Update conversion tests with new output~~ Locally fix conversion tests for now
- Closes https://github.com/ppy/osu/issues/22805

I've removed all usage of the legacy tick in the osu! ruleset. This makes things a lot more sane in my eyes:

- The tail is mapped to the tail now
- The judgement logic in `DrawableSlider` reads better

If we go in this direction, the stable `expected-conversion` code will need to be updated, as it no longer matches. This can be seen from the test failures on this PR currently.

If this is seen as an overbearing or otherwise unwanted change, then the last two commits (62bcb6284232833fbec4f30a8f79bfa635771ddf and dd6d09189e21d7a58df891823ba1daf9e8625c83) can be reverted.

Another direction I explored was removing the code from `SliderEventGenerator` completely – the only thing relying on it as of this PR is osu!catch conversion. You can see how this would look on [this branch](https://github.com/ppy/osu/compare/master...peppy:osu:legacy-tick-go-boom?expand=1). I stopped exploring this direction as it feels like this would be less legible (having hidden logic in `JuiceStream`) but others may have different opinions.

