I've made a final change which should bring 1:1 parity with diffcalc, if that's what we want. Any of the last three commits can be reverted depending on the decided direction.

I also attempted to fix the conversion mapping stuff (locally, just to see if it was simple) but I dunno if it's even feasible to get right. Here's what I have, but there are some new test failures which are probably related to the same thing as in the diffcalc logic and require similar fixes but to what end?

```diff
diff --git a/osu.Game.Rulesets.Osu.Tests/OsuBeatmapConversionTest.cs b/osu.Game.Rulesets.Osu.Tests/OsuBeatmapConversionTest.cs
index 11e69dc133..d2cba2a686 100644
--- a/osu.Game.Rulesets.Osu.Tests/OsuBeatmapConversionTest.cs
+++ b/osu.Game.Rulesets.Osu.Tests/OsuBeatmapConversionTest.cs
@@ -44,13 +44,25 @@ protected override IEnumerable<ConvertValue> CreateConvertValue(HitObject hitObj
                     break;
             }
 
-            static ConvertValue createConvertValue(OsuHitObject obj) => new ConvertValue
+            static ConvertValue createConvertValue(OsuHitObject obj)
             {
-                StartTime = obj.StartTime,
-                EndTime = obj.GetEndTime(),
-                X = obj.StackedPosition.X,
-                Y = obj.StackedPosition.Y
-            };
+                double startTime = obj.StartTime;
+                double endTime = obj.GetEndTime();
+
+                if (obj is SliderTailCircle)
+                {
+                    startTime += SliderEventGenerator.TAIL_LENIENCY;
+                    endTime += SliderEventGenerator.TAIL_LENIENCY;
+                }
+
+                return new ConvertValue
+                {
+                    StartTime = startTime,
+                    EndTime = endTime,
+                    X = obj.StackedPosition.X,
+                    Y = obj.StackedPosition.Y
+                };
+            }
         }
 
         protected override Ruleset CreateRuleset() => new OsuRuleset();

```

Two of the failures are fixed by

```diff
diff --git a/osu.Game.Rulesets.Osu.Tests/OsuBeatmapConversionTest.cs b/osu.Game.Rulesets.Osu.Tests/OsuBeatmapConversionTest.cs
